1.63.2 / September 26, 2026
[Alexandr Topilski]
- The line pinned under the page appears only when the shop promises something about delivery; a shop that states a return window alone no longer shows a bar with a "got it" button that closes nothing
- The footer states the terms on every page - free delivery from a sum, how fast, how long to return - from the same settings, whether or not the pinned line was closed

1.63.1 / September 26, 2026
[Alexandr Topilski]
- The new Storefront tab in the profile has its Save button: settings typed there could not be saved at all
- The subscription block keeps the page width instead of running edge to edge, and its field and button sit on one line

1.63.0 / September 26, 2026
[Alexandr Topilski]
- The catalogue page declares the shop's own search, so a search box can appear under the site in results; a search results page does not declare one
- Headings on a product card are h2, not h3: description, characteristics and set contents are page sections, and the ladder no longer skips a level
- The cart shows what delivery costs before the order: free above the threshold, the sum below it, and "we will tell you when we confirm" when the shop stated nothing
- Every page carries the shop's promise in one line - free delivery from a sum, how fast, how long to return - and the buyer can close it for good
- A public offer page, built from the shop's own settings, and a tick in the order that accepts it together with the privacy policy; the wording accepted is stored with the order
- Buyers can ask for the shop's letters: a form in the footer and an optional tick in the order, with one-click unsubscribe. The admin shows how many there are and exports them with the date, the source and the consent
- The shop's city and street address reach the organisation markup, which is what a local or AI answer is built from
- Schema: four columns added by hand (see below); the subscribers table is created on start
- Upgrade:
    ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN consent_at DATETIME;
    ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN consent_text TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
    ALTER TABLE settings ADD COLUMN shop_city TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
    ALTER TABLE settings ADD COLUMN shop_address TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';

1.62.0 / September 26, 2026
[Alexandr Topilski]
- Delivery and returns are structured data: four numbers in the profile (delivery cost, free from, delivery days, return days) and the product card carries OfferShippingDetails and MerchantReturnPolicy. Answer engines and rich results read fields, not the owner's prose on the delivery page; a field left at zero is not stated and prints nothing
- The delivery country comes from the shop currency, so there is nothing else to fill in

Upgrading a live shop needs four columns added by hand:

    ALTER TABLE settings ADD COLUMN delivery_cost INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
    ALTER TABLE settings ADD COLUMN delivery_free_from INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
    ALTER TABLE settings ADD COLUMN delivery_days INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
    ALTER TABLE settings ADD COLUMN return_days INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;

